sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant H as Handler
    participant S as Store
    participant R as Redis
    participant M as Sub Manager
    C->>H: POST /chat + body
    H->>H: authorize path · parse content type, producer headers, sequence, and close flag
    H->>S: Store.Get(path) · existence, write class, content type, tail
    S->>R: HGETALL :meta + :prod · one pipeline
    H->>S: handleAppend → Store.Append(path, data, opts) · TailHint = the tail Get returned
    Note over S: frame JSON or binary bytes against the hinted tail · no second read
    S->>R: EVALSHA append.lua
    Note over S,R: atomic validate → tail == expected? → ZADD → HSET tail → PUBLISH
    R-->>S: reply OK, newTail — or RETRY carrying the live tail
    alt tail moved before the script
        S->>R: reframe against the live tail · EVALSHA again, at most 128 attempts
    end
    S-->>H: typed append result and producer result
    H->>H: map duplicate, fence, conflict, close, and success headers
    H->>M: OnStreamAppend(path) after a new durable append
    Note over H,M: enqueue or coalesce one path<br/>fixed 1,024-entry local queue · no Redis call
    M-->>H: bounded enqueue outcome
    H-->>C: 200 or 204 · Stream-Next-Offset 0_29
    Note over H,M: worker evaluates subscribers independently
